Today, we’re diving into one of the most powerful concepts used in web development and automation testing
1.Element Selector
p {
  color: blue;
}

2.ID Selector
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    #mainBox {
      background-color: orange;
      color: white;
      padding: 10px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div id="mainBox">I am styled using ID selector</div>
  <div>I am not affected</div>

</body>
</html>

3.Class Selector
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    .box {
      background-color: lightblue;
      border: 1px solid blue;
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 5px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="box">Box 1</div>
  <div class="box">Box 2</div>
  <div class="box">Box 3</div>
  <div>I'm a normal div</div>

</body>
</html>

